Fri Jul 19 11:44:58 2024 Alan Dayton
v1.49.18
Reviewers: David Dawson, Peter Robinson (He/Him), Ben Liu

* The verifyCompletedReview publish step now checks submodules and subprojects as well as the top level
* To pass the check, a pull request must exist, the pull request must be approved by the required number of approvers, and the required number of approvers must be greater than 0
* The author info is still pulled from the top level pull request, but the list of reviewers saved by grape for reporting purposes is now a union of the set of reviewers from each pull request

Example output showing what is reported if each condition is not met:
'''
GRAPE: Code reviews are not completed in the following repo(s):
	<path/to>/test_submodule_1: Needs pull request (run grape review)
	<path/to>/test_subproject_1: Needs reviewers (run grape review)
	test_application_1: Needs review from Alan Dayton
'''

Example output showing what is reported if all checks pass:
'''
GRAPE: All reviewers have approved your request.
'''

This was tested using the test_application_1 repo, which has test_submodule_1 as a submodule and test_subproject_1 as a subproject. All three of these repos are now part of the Grape group for use in future testing.


